  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Occasional rain today and tonight, with the \ngreater totals Downeast.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nSurface low pressure slowly tracks across the southern Gulf of \nMaine today through tonight, while the supporting upper low \ncrosses the region. Occasional rain will occur across the region\ntoday through early tonight, then diminish overnight. Isolated \nthunderstorms are also possible, mostly Downeast. The greater \nrainfall totals today through tonight will generally occur \nacross Downeast areas, with lesser totals northward across the \nremainder of the forecast area. Rainfall totals are generally \nexpected to range from a tenth to quarter inch north, with \naround quarter to third of an inch across central areas with \naround a third to a half inch Downeast. However, local \nvariations in these totals will occur.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Showers and thunderstorms likely this weekend \ninto early next week.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2 DESCRIPTION... \nA cold front approaches our area Saturday with an area of low \npressure developing along it Saturday night. The low should pass\nnorth of our area Sunday into Monday. Showers and a few \nisolated thunderstorms possible over the North Woods Saturday as\nthe cold front approaches with more showers and a greater \nlikelihood for thunderstorms Sunday as low pressure passes to \nour north. The greatest chance for storms will be over northern \nand western Maine as southerly flow is likely to keep stable \nmarine air over more southern and eastern areas. Models \ngenerally show several hundred J/kg of instability but are still\nuncertain on exact amounts. Thus, limited confidence in storm \nseverity at this time.",
